  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "31435408",
      "title": "Converting Picked Locations to Human-Readable Addresses",
      "lectureOrder": 210,
      "videoOrder": 204,
      "sourceHash": "38cfca81cfadc191119d62ff5fc25aeff0ab854ae1553a507bd57b59f5bd12da",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.316,
          "end": 3.83,
          "en": "[Maximilian Schwarzmuller] So how can we convert",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.83,
          "end": 7.63,
          "en": "such a pickedLocation to a human readable address?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.63,
          "end": 11.8,
          "en": "We can again use an API provided by Google.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.8,
          "end": 14.78,
          "en": "In this case, the geocoding API",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.78,
          "end": 17.893,
          "en": "which you can find if you search for Google maps geocode.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.13,
          "end": 23.73,
          "en": "Now this is another API to which we can send http requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 23.73,
          "end": 26.12,
          "en": "And this is an API which allows us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 26.12,
          "end": 28.84,
          "en": "to translate addresses to coordinates",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.84,
          "end": 31.27,
          "en": "and coordinates to addresses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.27,
          "end": 34.127,
          "en": "The latter is called reverse geocoding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.23,
          "end": 39.41,
          "en": "Now we already did create a Google cloud platform project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 39.41,
          "end": 43.86,
          "en": "so we can easily get started here with this geocoding API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 43.86,
          "end": 46.01,
          "en": "We just need to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 46.01,
          "end": 49.023,
          "en": "that we actually have this API enabled.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 50.02,
          "end": 52.57,
          "en": "For that, if you're logged into your Google account,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 52.57,
          "end": 54.87,
          "en": "under APIs, you should make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 54.87,
          "end": 57.56,
          "en": "that the geocoding API is enabled.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 57.56,
          "end": 60.71,
          "en": "And then we can use the same API key as before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 60.71,
          "end": 63.62,
          "en": "to talk to that API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 63.62,
          "end": 65.55,
          "en": "For that, of course, you should make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 65.55,
          "end": 70.55,
          "en": "that under credentials for this project you have an API key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 71.13,
          "end": 72.86,
          "en": "In this case, I even have two,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 72.86,
          "end": 74.52,
          "en": "but you should at least have one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.52,
          "end": 78.41,
          "en": "And that's the API key you want to use here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 78.41,
          "end": 80.47,
          "en": "for getting that map preview.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.47,
          "end": 83.41,
          "en": "And that's also the API key we will use now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.41,
          "end": 87.76,
          "en": "for translating a location or a pair of coordinates",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 87.76,
          "end": 89.65299999999999,
          "en": "into a human readable address.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 90.73,
          "end": 93.83,
          "en": "To do that, back in our code in the util folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 93.83,
          "end": 96.53999999999999,
          "en": "and they are in the location.js file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 96.53999999999999,
          "end": 98.34,
          "en": "we can export a number function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 98.34,
          "end": 100.3,
          "en": "which could be called getAddress.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 101.624,
          "end": 104.07,
          "en": "And this function wants to get a latitude",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 104.07,
          "end": 106.83,
          "en": "and a longitude coordinate as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 106.83,
          "end": 108.56,
          "en": "It will be a async function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 108.56,
          "end": 111.7,
          "en": "because I want to use await in this function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 111.7,
          "end": 114.57,
          "en": "because in here I wanna send a http request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 114.57,
          "end": 116.07,
          "en": "with the fetch function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 116.07,
          "end": 118.17,
          "en": "which is built into JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 118.17,
          "end": 121.5,
          "en": "also available here in React Native apps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 121.5,
          "end": 125.2,
          "en": "Alternatively, we could also install Axios again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 125.2,
          "end": 128.49,
          "en": "which is a third party library we used before in the course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 128.49,
          "end": 131.21,
          "en": "for sending http requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 131.21,
          "end": 132.47,
          "en": "In order to show both,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 132.47,
          "end": 136.3,
          "en": "I'm going to use to built-in fetch API instead here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 136.3,
          "end": 139.98,
          "en": "So fetch allows us to send http requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 139.98,
          "end": 143.77,
          "en": "And if you go back to the geocoding API documentation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 143.77,
          "end": 148.03,
          "en": "you also learn where to send requests to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 148.03,
          "end": 150.87,
          "en": "In our case, it's the reverse geocoding request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 150.87,
          "end": 152.57999999999998,
          "en": "which you wanna send.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 152.57999999999998,
          "end": 155.57999999999998,
          "en": "Now, here we learn all the details about this request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 155.57999999999998,
          "end": 159.393,
          "en": "including the URL to which the request should be sent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 160.47,
          "end": 162.19,
          "en": "So we can copy that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 162.19,
          "end": 166.6,
          "en": "and then construct this URL here in our code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 166.6,
          "end": 169.78,
          "en": "So here again, I will use a template literal with backticks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 169.78,
          "end": 172.27,
          "en": "so that we can inject data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 172.27,
          "end": 174.23,
          "en": "And then here we have to inject",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 174.23,
          "end": 177.64,
          "en": "our actual latitude and long coordinates,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 177.64,
          "end": 179.26,
          "en": "starting with the latitude",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 179.26,
          "end": 183.23,
          "en": "and then followed with the longitude.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 183.23,
          "end": 185.61,
          "en": "So these are the two parameters we're getting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 185.61,
          "end": 187.33,
          "en": "injected into that string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 187.33,
          "end": 192.33,
          "en": "separated by a comma after this latlng query parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 193.31,
          "end": 197.06,
          "en": "And here at the end, we also inject our API key,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 197.06,
          "end": 199.96,
          "en": "the Google API key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 199.96,
          "end": 203.3,
          "en": "That's the URL we now wanna send a request to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 203.3,
          "end": 205.77,
          "en": "And we wanna send a regular get request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 205.77,
          "end": 208.5,
          "en": "and you can learn more details about the request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 208.5,
          "end": 210.77,
          "en": "and the response that will be returned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 210.77,
          "end": 212.963,
          "en": "in the official documentation, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 214,
          "end": 218.56,
          "en": "Now here, I will simply pass my URL to fetch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 218.56,
          "end": 223.09,
          "en": "and then await the result of that to get my response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 223.09,
          "end": 226.32999999999998,
          "en": "That's how the fetch API works, the fetch function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 226.32999999999998,
          "end": 228.7,
          "en": "It gives us such a response object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 228.7,
          "end": 231.853,
          "en": "once the promise generated by fetch resolved.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 233.06,
          "end": 236.43,
          "en": "Now, I then wanna check if my response is maybe not okay,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 236.43,
          "end": 238.99,
          "en": "which we can do with the built-in okay property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 238.99,
          "end": 240.86,
          "en": "on this response object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 240.86,
          "end": 243.86,
          "en": "And if it is not okay, if we got an error code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 243.86,
          "end": 246,
          "en": "then I wanna throw a new error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 246,
          "end": 249.27,
          "en": "where I say failed to fetch address,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 249.27,
          "end": 250.76,
          "en": "so that we also handle the case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 250.76,
          "end": 253.333,
          "en": "that we get back an error response code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 254.95,
          "end": 256.64,
          "en": "If we make it past this if check,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 256.64,
          "end": 259.13,
          "en": "we know that we successfully sent a request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 259.13,
          "end": 260.77,
          "en": "to Google's API endpoint",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 260.77,
          "end": 263.413,
          "en": "and that we get back some address data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 264.32,
          "end": 266.82,
          "en": "So now we can get our response data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 266.82,
          "end": 270.12,
          "en": "by calling the json method on the response object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 270.12,
          "end": 273.13,
          "en": "and awaiting that, because json returns a promise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 273.13,
          "end": 277.55,
          "en": "which eventually resolves to the actual response data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 277.55,
          "end": 281.4,
          "en": "And then we can get the address by diving into this data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 281.4,
          "end": 284.85,
          "en": "and there into the results array which we'll find in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 284.85,
          "end": 286.82,
          "en": "And then the first result,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 286.82,
          "end": 290.093,
          "en": "and there, the formatted address.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 291.44,
          "end": 292.92,
          "en": "How do I know that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 292.92,
          "end": 296.04,
          "en": "Well, I know that because of the official docs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 296.04,
          "end": 299.15,
          "en": "That's the kind of response we'll get back.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 299.15,
          "end": 302.51,
          "en": "There will be a results array in the response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 302.51,
          "end": 305.26,
          "en": "and we can then get the first element of that array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 305.26,
          "end": 308.73,
          "en": "And in there, we will find a formatted address field",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 308.73,
          "end": 311.73,
          "en": "which gives us the human readable address.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 311.73,
          "end": 314.103,
          "en": "And that's exactly what I'm extracting here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 315.08,
          "end": 317.67,
          "en": "And then in the end, I returned this address here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 317.67,
          "end": 321,
          "en": "as part of the get address helper function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 321,
          "end": 322.73,
          "en": "Since this is a async function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 322.73,
          "end": 324.76,
          "en": "we will actually return a promise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 324.76,
          "end": 328.29,
          "en": "but that promise will eventually resolve to this address.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 328.29,
          "end": 330.08,
          "en": "Or in case of any errors,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 330.08,
          "end": 333.133,
          "en": "it will be rejected with the appropriate error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 334.09000000000003,
          "end": 337.15999999999997,
          "en": "So now we can use this getAddress helper function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 337.15999999999997,
          "end": 340.23,
          "en": "to translate coordinates to an address.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 340.23,
          "end": 342.783,
          "en": "The question just is where we want to do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 344.22,
          "end": 346.1,
          "en": "And there will be different ways",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 346.1,
          "end": 348.01,
          "en": "and different places of doing that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 348.01,
          "end": 351.05,
          "en": "but I think the LocationPicker is a good place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 351.05,
          "end": 352.24,
          "en": "for doing that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 352.24,
          "end": 354.15,
          "en": "Specifically in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 354.15,
          "end": 357.15999999999997,
          "en": "we already have some code that executes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 357.15999999999997,
          "end": 359.63,
          "en": "whenever the pickedLocation changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 359.63,
          "end": 361.363,
          "en": "This useEffect code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 362.36,
          "end": 364.9,
          "en": "I would argue that this is a great place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 364.9,
          "end": 367.75,
          "en": "for then translating this pickedLocation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 367.75,
          "end": 370.03,
          "en": "which is a pair of coordinates,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 370.03,
          "end": 373.09,
          "en": "a pair of latitude longitude coordinates",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 373.09,
          "end": 377.38,
          "en": "into a more complex object that still has these coordinates",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 377.38,
          "end": 379.663,
          "en": "but also a human readable address.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 380.65,
          "end": 382.84,
          "en": "And therefore, in here in this useEffect call",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 382.84,
          "end": 386.58,
          "en": "we can check if pickedLocation is truthy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 386.58,
          "end": 388.67,
          "en": "So, if we do have a location.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 388.67,
          "end": 390.41,
          "en": "And if that is the case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 390.41,
          "end": 393.94,
          "en": "I wanna eventually call on pickedLocation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 393.94,
          "end": 396.383,
          "en": "but I also want to call getAddress.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 397.27,
          "end": 401.13,
          "en": "And getAddress is this helper function we just worked on",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
